transformationAnalysis.body:
Traditional validation frameworks compile into massive blocks of inline JavaScript variables, dragging thousands of duplicate lines of property trees straight into your production bundles. Xalor solves this by executing **Structural Type Eradication** during the AST traversal phase.

### 🔄 The Before vs. After Structural Change

```ts
// 📦 1. Before Compilation (Your Source Code File)
type User = { id: string; email: string };
registerXalor<'USER', User>();

const validData = xalor.validate<'USER', 'parse'>(rawData);
```

```js
// 🚀 2. After Compilation (The Eradicated Build Artifact Output)
// The heavy User structural parameters and nominal generic blocks disappear entirely!
const validData = xalor.validate('USER', 'parse', rawData);
```

### 📊 Performance and Safety Guarantees:
* **True Tree-Shaking Purity:** Because type structures are completely erased rather than converted into bulky runtime JS objects, your production bundlers (Vite, Rollup, Webpack) never inherit code bloat from un-executed properties.
* **Production Code Security:** Eradicating the structural type metadata from the compiled source means malicious reverse-engineering threads cannot reconstruct your private API contracts or database models simply by inspecting your client bundle files.
